      ":question/problem": "The growth rate of the fish population $P(t)$ in a certain lake is jointly proportional to the fish population at time $t$, measured in years, and the difference between the lake's carrying capacity and the fish population. If the constant of proportionality is $0.0003$ and the carrying capacity is $5000$, then find an expression for the fish population after $t$ years, given that there were $1000$ fish in the lake initially.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
